<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Greece.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Greece</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The monarchy is abolished; it is restored by plebiscite in 1935</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/islam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Republic of Turkey abolishes the Ottoman caliphate</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/indus-valley-civilisation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indus%20Valley%20Civilisation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indus Valley Civilisation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Marshall announces the discovery of a forgotten civilisation of the Indus</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/dong-son-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dong%20Son%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dong Son culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A fisherman, Nguyễn Văn Lắm, reports bronze finds to the École française d’Extrême-Orient, and excavations begin at Đông Sơn village</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/harlem-renaissance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Harlem%20Renaissance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Harlem Renaissance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Opportunity: A Journal of Negro Life holds a party for Black writers attended by many white publishers</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/kemalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kemalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kemalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ottoman caliphate is abolished, and the office of Shaykh al-Islām is replaced by the Presidency of Religious Affairs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Turkish National Assembly abolishes the Caliphate, shocking the Sunni clerical world</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/northern-rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Northern%20Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Northern Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 1 April the British Government takes over the administration, with Herbert Stanley as governor and Livingstone as capital</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-polish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Polish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Polish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Prime Minister Władysław Grabski introduces the złoty, which brings the hyperinflation under control without foreign loans or aid</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mustafa-kemal-ataturk"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mustafa%20Kemal%20Atat%C3%BCrk.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The caliphate is abolished and its powers transferred to the Grand National Assembly; sharia courts are closed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/quran"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quran.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quran</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Al-Azhar University publishes the Cairo edition, which standardises Quranic orthography and became the basis of later editions</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mecca"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mecca.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mecca</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Saud family takes Mecca and overthrows the sharif</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/bukhara"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bukhara.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bukhara</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bukharan People's Soviet Republic is integrated into the Uzbek Soviet Socialist Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mohenjo-daro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mohenjo-daro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mohenjo-daro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Large-scale excavations begin under Kashinath Dikshit, followed by John Marshall in 1925</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/statue-of-liberty"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Statue%20of%20Liberty.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Statue of Liberty</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">President Calvin Coolidge declared the statue a national monument</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/panchatantra"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Panchatantra.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Panchatantra</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Franklin Edgerton publishes his reconstruction of the original Sanskrit text</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/vladimir-lenin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vladimir%20Lenin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vladimir Lenin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lenin dies at Gorki and is laid in a mausoleum on Red Square</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/yaa-asantewaa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Yaa%20Asantewaa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Yaa Asantewaa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Prempeh I and the other exiles are allowed to return to Asante, and her remains are returned for a royal burial</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/surrealism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Surrealism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Surrealism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yvan Goll publishes his Manifeste du surréalisme on 1 October and Breton publishes his on 15 October</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Rabindranath Tagore lectures in China and warns that it could encounter trouble by integrating too much progressive and foreign thought</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/wahhabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wahhabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wahhabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud and his army conquer Mecca</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/stalinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Stalinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Stalinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Stalin first develops the idea of socialism in one country, elaborating it in his writings of 1925–26</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The abolition of the caliphate leads pan-Islamism to mobilise Muslim masses inspired by Rida’s ideas</span></li></ul></section>
